l":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/12545","id":1096107251,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAGuhRc5BVUTz","user":{"login":"Kurt-von-Laven","id":974910,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3NDkxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/974910?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kurt-von-Laven","html_url":"https://github.com/Kurt-von-Laven","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kurt-von-Laven/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kurt-von-Laven/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kurt-von-Laven/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kurt-von-Laven/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kurt-von-Laven/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kurt-von-Laven/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kurt-von-Laven/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kurt-von-Laven/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Kurt-von-Laven/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-04-12T05:50:25Z","updated_at":"2022-05-11T19:46:54Z","body":"Not sure whether this is related or separate, but I experience the same symptom in the following scenario:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nfrom typing import Any\r\n\r\ndef test_structural_pattern_matching(x: Any) -> Any:\r\n    match x:\r\n        case {\"x\": {\"y\": [value]}}:\r\n            print(\"mypy believes this line is unreachable\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nHappy to file a separate issue if desired. Intriguingly, if you remove the outer dictionary, mypy stops complaining. This bug particularly impacts the use of structural pattern matching in code that handles JSON, which obviously frequently contains complex nested data structures.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/1096107251/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,